,"abstract":[{"text":"Glissando and slide types both indicate rapidly moving from one pitch to the other so that individual notes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are not discerned. A slide is continuous between the two pitches and defaults to a solid line. The optional","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"text for a slide is printed alongside the line.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSlide"}],"title":"MXLSlide"}}}